      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report a case of a 65-year-old man with newly diagnosed squamous carcinoma of the lung, who presented with worsening left-knee pain. A bone scintigraphy displayed an increased radioactivity in the left patella. The patient underwent left patellectomy. Histopathological examination revealed metastasis to the patella from the known lung cancer."},
